WEBVTT

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:05.560
<i>I'm outside?</i>

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:08.590
<i>Why? What was I doing?</i>

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:10.320
<i>Did I eat breakfast alrea—</i>

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.260
<i>No, this is Mars.</i>

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.610
<i>That's right, I was in the lake...</i>

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:31.050
<i>That's right.</i>

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.140
I'm starting to remember now.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.810
It was this right hand, wasn't it?

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:59.000
String?

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.330
I see.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.420
So Akari saved me.

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:33.900
Wh-Why you... What did you do to Akari?

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:35.970
To my friend?!

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.010
Wha?

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.820
Ow...

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:42.690
Oh, Michelle-san!

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.120
Thank goodness you're safe!

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:47.740
R-Right...

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.090
Whoa, there.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.090
This guy still wants to go at it?

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:03.260
I apologize.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:05.490
I did manage to catch this thing,

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:08.230
but I accidentally let it go.

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:11.620
Oh, Alex is guarding everyone else.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:13.170
There have been no casualties.

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.990
You're still winded, 
aren't you, Michelle-san?

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:17.940
I'll take care of things here—

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:20.970
Who'd you say was winded?

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.810
You're all wobbly, too.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:26.290
And your coat stinks.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:27.620
Jeez.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.250
I take it back, Akari.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.260
You're not a good subordinate.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:39.850
Ow!

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:40.710
You're a good man.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.520
<i>Pray, if God even exists on Mars.</i>

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:12.710
We've successfully captured

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.600
two BUGS-type terraformars.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:50.990
<b><i>Brave Warrior</i></b>

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:06.770
S-Sorry.

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:10.340
I made a U-turn while that guy was dangling.

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:18.290
U-Um, also, right before we landed,
 we received a transmission.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.010
It was an SOS.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.770
From where?

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:23.590
From the Rome No. 6 Division,

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.870
and the Japanese and American No. 1 Division.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:36.800
All right. Thankfully the power 
and radio are still fine.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.780
The bug cage isn't broken, either.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:41.850
U-Um, I really am sorry.

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:42.780
It's fine.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.950
Everyone's alive thanks to you.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:46.780
Though...

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:49.040
we won't be able to fly this thing anymore.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:53.320
U-Um, there's one other thing...

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:56.540
Earlier, my ears were ringing 
so I couldn't hear it very well, but...

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:00.540
What did you say after
 "You're not a good subordinate"?

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:01.820
Oh.

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:04.000
I said you're a pig bastard.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:05.170
Oh...

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:08.540
Anyway, we can fix the wheels at least.

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:10.550
We're going to have to use this thing to move.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.060
Change these tires.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:20.820
You know how, don't you?

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:22.450
Yeah, pretty much.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.590
Don't let your guard down 
about your surroundings, either.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:25.320
Right.

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:28.210
I'm going to change behind that rock there.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:29.570
It wouldn't be funny if we

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.080
came all the way to Mars
 just for me to catch a cold and die.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:33.280
I'll be right back.

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:39.860
Yaeko, please!

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:41.730
At least let us look in that direction.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:43.630
No! These are the division leader's orders!

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:47.360
So this is how you repay me 
for saving your life...

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:49.630
Well then, Yaeko...

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:51.740
I'll give you five thousand.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:57.570
You could go to a pizza buffet twice.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:59.730
Three times, if it's lunch.

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:06.520
Do you think you can buy
 a Japanese beauty like myself with that?

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:08.370
This is the problem with cheap men.

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.360
Yaeko-chan.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.420
Fifty thousand.

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:12.990
Wha?!

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:15.620
Fifty thousand?! Are you insane?!

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:18.290
You idiot, it's Michelle-san!

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.450
She's not like one of those girls you can catch

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:22.080
in Shinjuku just by casting a net.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.670
She's got actual blonde hair and yet...

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:27.000
And yet...

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.560
She doesn't have her 
naval pierced! I don't think...

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:31.020
But she's blonde...

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:33.890
H-Huh? I got something in my eye...

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.660
I can't see a thing.

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:36.660
Those damn cockroaches.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:41.750
<i>Neither of the divisions responded...</i>

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.120
<i>Are they in the middle of 
battling cockroaches, too?</i>

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.990
<i>I've got a bad feeling about this.</i>

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:51.330
<i>Something is happening on Mars.</i>

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:54.130
<i>Something other than 
the war against the roaches...</i>

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:57.280
<i>It feels like something more is happening.</i>

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:27.980
Hypothesis number one.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:31.180
In regards to why you guys were

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:33.490
insects with six legs just five hundred years ago,

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:40.600
but somehow evolved into bipeds 
that resemble slightly buff cavemen.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.750
Want to hear it?

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:49.380
There's really no way this would 
have happened via natural selection.

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:56.620
Despite your appearances, 
you all have quite a high ability to learn,

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:59.510
and your aggression towards humans...

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:04.010
It's definitely artificial.

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:11.000
According to Alexander Gustav Newton, who was in charge of the BUGS 2...

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:14.490
There were visitors prior to us trying to terraform.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.660
However, this theory...

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:42.510
You're rather impatient.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:50.360
All right, I'll explain it in even simpler terms.

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:53.480
Because of you guys,

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:58.270
Earth is a mess right now.

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:01.220
Hey...

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.210
You should probably stop calling yourself "Papa."

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:09.420
You're going to be a grandpa, now.

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:13.420
Grandpa.

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:26.890
<i>If you're not going to bring out who's in charge,</i>

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:32.590
<i>you can die first.</i>

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:37.030
<b><i></i>Martian Atmosphere and Roach Suitability Ranking<i></i></b>

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:38.200
<b>3rd</b>

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:40.030
<b>Sylvester Asimov</b>

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.030
<b>Martian Atmosphere and Roach Suitability Ranking 3rd</b>

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.670
<i>The shells of the crustaceans in the ocean</i>

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:52.350
<i>are high in calcium and very hard</i>

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:55.300
<i>compared to those of insects,
 because they need to</i>

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.580
<i>withstand water pressure.</i>

00:10:58.140 --> 00:10:59.920
<i>They are also very thick.</i>

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:02.310
<i>There is also a part</i>

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:04.680
<i>of their shells that has a mechanism
 called defensive autotomy.</i>

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:07.200
<i>In the case of emergency, it is well-known</i>

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:10.420
<i>that they will amputate their own pincers or legs.</i>

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.940
<i>Of course, there is also the fact 
that they can regenerate.</i>

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:33.420
It's a bit thin.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:36.020
I guess I'll have to strengthen it again.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:50.770
There's no assurance that 
everyone in the crew are combatants...

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:54.600
If this was any other country.

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:57.190
There are ten enemies!

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:59.190
From here on out, sign A.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:01.070
The enemies of humanity,

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:02.820
the ones responsible for your sister's death,

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:04.820
and...

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:10.950
the bastards that spread that virus to my daughter.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:14.750
Here we go, assholes!

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:52.790
Hey, now...

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:58.290
Hey, now. Seriously? Is that all you've got?

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:05.130
You stupid bugs.

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:14.490
You don't feel pain or fear.

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:17.020
That's why you never learn.

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:18.920
You assholes!

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:27.240
Ivan, are you done?

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:37.210
Why, you...!

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:12.790
Say, Ivan...

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:15.790
What kind of dreams do you think this thing is seeing?

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:19.540
Who knows? Perhaps...

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:22.130
A dream

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:25.120
where it's having some alien child
 heal the wound on its finger...

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:28.300
No, sorry. That was a joke.

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:33.310
They lost as soon as they tried to get
 closer to us intelligent creatures.

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:37.240
On Earth, there is plenty of grass you can't eat

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:40.310
despite how green and delicious it may look.

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:45.760
Learn the feeling of regret
 while you're stuck in your delusion.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:53.640
<i>The devil's trumpet...</i>

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:56.680
<i>A plant belonging to the Solanaceae family,
 that grows in Central America.</i>

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:02.030
<i>All parts of this plant contain
 the hallucinogen </i>tropane alkaloid.<i></i>

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:06.130
<i>Depending on how much is absorbed,
 it can cause fever</i>

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:07.970
<i>and can cause the autonomic nerves,</i>

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:11.060
<i>breathing, and the heart to all stop functioning.</i>

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.290
Whoa, there.

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:46.590
Like I'm going to let you go.

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:51.500
I know that your central nerves function

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:55.850
the same as when you were just roaches.

00:15:59.550 --> 00:16:03.580
Meaning, control of your whole body
 doesn't come from your head,

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:06.980
but from the suboesophageal 
ganglion in your chest.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:09.830
That's why, even if your head gets chopped off,

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:12.820
there are times your body can keep moving.

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:16.160
As long as your subesophageal ganglion is safe

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:19.180
and the passage to your lungs remains open.

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:25.500
However, it's different if I crush your throat.

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:29.480
Say...

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:33.240
You don't feel pain, right?

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:36.760
Why are you hitting me, then?

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:39.280
Do you feel for your comrade?

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:44.400
Is it your orders? 
Or do you just think we're gross?

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:48.500
You see, you roach bastards...

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:52.780
My daughter is in U-NASA's hospital ward.

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:33.280
I'm going to protect the country
 she's going home to, as well.

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:41.170
I don't care if the terrorists that threaten her

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:45.420
peace are viruses or cockroaches,
 or even some ancient civilization.

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:48.830
I'm going to find them and 
chase them down as far as I need to...

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:56.230
Even if they're just hiding in the bathroom...

00:17:56.230 --> 00:17:58.340
I will kill them.

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:24.450
Commander.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:29.280
This thing doesn't know front from back right now,

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:31.460
but it'll probably regain its senses soon.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:36.200
I'm not very good with how much
 alkaloid I should be exuding...

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:41.190
Please

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:44.810
let me have the launcher.

00:18:54.510 --> 00:18:56.640
Target captured.

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.290
We are detaining two terraformars.

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:13.030
<i>Sis...</i>

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:17.370
By the way,

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:20.720
I wonder if the fact they looked
 like they were trying to run away

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:23.550
at the last minute was 
only due to a random decision.

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:27.680
No, they could have actually
 got it into their heads...

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:30.690
That humans are scary.

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:34.060
Especially Russians.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:36.760
We're going in.

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:45.240
It's already night...

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:49.940
Adolf...

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:53.330
I see.

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:56.350
From the No. 1 Division and the No. 6 Division...

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:59.340
Should we try heading toward
 one of them to assist them?

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:04.430
No. You should head
 to the crash site of the Annex 1.

00:20:04.730 --> 00:20:09.480
This is urgent, Adolf. 
Get there before China or Russia.

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:11.800
<i>Understood.</i>

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:13.950
I'm counting on you.

00:20:17.130 --> 00:20:18.490
Seriously?

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:20.540
We're going to retrieve the roof.

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:54.870
I'd heard about it,

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:57.720
but to think it's raining as 
much as it would on Earth...

00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:00.250
I'm worried about the acid rain.

00:21:01.550 --> 00:21:03.270
What's that?

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:08.900
Isn't that...

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:17.630
What? Fatty tuna? The special?

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:22.000
Go for it. Eat as much as you'd like.

00:21:23.400 --> 00:21:25.630
We haven't run into any cockroaches...

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:29.010
Cockroaches on Earth are nocturnal, aren't they?

00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:33.020
Yeah. As long as they've inherited that...

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:36.520
That means their time is just starting.

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:40.410
<b><i>The Electric Organism</i></b>
